{"id": 37, "ts": 1780780853.4345472, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I appreciate the points raised about D\u2019s solid technical profile, but the new evidence about Candidate\u202fC changes the balance. We now know C \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis,\u201d which directly addresses the stress\u2011resilience gap we had for C, and the note that C \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere with his crew\u201d gives us concrete proof of crew cooperation\u2014something we still lack for D. Moreover, C \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly\u201d and has \u201cexcellent attention skills,\u201d covering decision quality and information accuracy, while also \u201cputs concern for others above everything,\u201d supporting responsibility and a collaborative mindset. The concerns about C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas and an egocentric attitude are real, yet the positive crew\u2011atmosphere observation suggests these traits have not yet impaired teamwork. In contrast, D\u2019s moodiness and loner perception remain unverified but could affect cockpit interaction, and we have no evidence of his crew\u2011cooperation. Compared with B, C now meets all critical safety criteria without the memory\u2011deficit risk. Therefore, I shift my provisional recommendation to Candidate\u202fC as the best overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
